# {{ ansible_managed }} (backup/pbs-deploy)
# Client metrics (pbs_backup_*) come from each host's node_exporter textfile collector,
# written by the backup jobs themselves; server metrics (pbs_*) from pbs-exporter.
groups:
  - name: backup
    rules:
      - alert: BackupStale
        expr: time() - pbs_backup_last_success_timestamp_seconds{kind!="restore"} > {{ pbs_stale_hours | int }} * 3600
        for: 15m
        labels: { severity: warning }
        annotations:
          summary: "{% raw %}No good {{ $labels.kind }} backup of {{ $labels.target }} on {{ $labels.instance }}{% endraw %} for over {{ pbs_stale_hours }} hours"
          description: "{% raw %}journalctl -u pbs-backup-{{ $labels.kind }}.service on {{ $labels.instance }}{% endraw %}"
      - alert: RestoreTestStale
        expr: time() - pbs_backup_last_success_timestamp_seconds{kind="restore"} > {{ pbs_restore_stale_days | int }} * 86400
        for: 1h
        labels: { severity: warning }
        annotations:
          summary: "{% raw %}No passing restore test on {{ $labels.instance }} for over {% endraw %}{{ pbs_restore_stale_days }}{% raw %} days{% endraw %}"
          description: "{% raw %}journalctl -u pbs-restore-test.service on {{ $labels.instance }}{% endraw %}"
      - alert: BackupFailed
        expr: pbs_backup_last_exit_code != 0
        for: 5m
        labels: { severity: warning }
        annotations:
          summary: "{% raw %}Last {{ $labels.kind }} backup of {{ $labels.target }} on {{ $labels.instance }} failed (exit {{ $value }}){% endraw %}"
      - alert: BackupMetricsMissing
        expr: absent(pbs_backup_last_success_timestamp_seconds)
        for: 30h
        labels: { severity: warning }
        annotations:
          summary: "No backup job metrics at all (textfile collector, or no job ever succeeded)"
      - alert: PBSDown
        expr: up{job="pbs"} == 0 or pbs_up == 0
        for: 10m
        labels: { severity: critical }
        annotations:
          summary: "Proxmox Backup Server {{ pbs_fqdn }} is not answering the exporter"
      - alert: PBSDatastoreFilling
        expr: 100 * pbs_used / pbs_size > {{ pbs_store_full_pct | int }}
        for: 30m
        labels: { severity: warning }
        annotations:
          summary: "{% raw %}PBS datastore {{ $labels.datastore }} is {{ $value | printf \"%.0f\" }}% full{% endraw %}"
      # pbs_snapshot_vm_last_verify is the verify STATE of a group's newest snapshot (1 = ok, 0 = not
      # verified or failed), not a time. The verify job runs nightly on the local store, so a newest
      # snapshot still unverified after 30 h means the job isn't running or the snapshot fails it.
      # The offsite store is verified monthly by design: not covered here.
      - alert: PBSVerifyOverdue
        expr: pbs_snapshot_vm_last_verify{datastore="{{ pbs_datastore }}"} != 1
        for: 30h
        labels: { severity: warning }
        annotations:
          summary: "{% raw %}{{ $labels.vm_id }} in {{ $labels.datastore }}/{{ $labels.namespace }}: newest snapshot not verified OK for 30 h{% endraw %}"
{% if pbs_offsite_enabled | bool %}
      - alert: OffsiteBehind
        expr: |
          max by (namespace, vm_id) (pbs_snapshot_vm_last_timestamp{datastore="{{ pbs_datastore }}"})
            - on (namespace, vm_id)
          max by (namespace, vm_id) (pbs_snapshot_vm_last_timestamp{datastore="{{ pbs_offsite_store }}"})
            > 2 * 86400
        for: 2h
        labels: { severity: warning }
        annotations:
          summary: "{% raw %}Offsite copy of {{ $labels.vm_id }} ({{ $labels.namespace }}) is over 2 days behind the local datastore{% endraw %}"
          description: "Check the sync job {{ pbs_offsite_store }}-sync in the PBS UI (Datastore > {{ pbs_offsite_store }} > Sync Jobs)."
{% endif %}
